<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Otto's home 3: the founder's Mac, on local silicon (founder order 2026-09-09, "otto must
  have 3 homes"; THE MEDIC LAW, "it runs on local silicon (Ollama) ... when the cluster or
  router is down, the medic must still be fully able to think").

  Ollama.app binds 127.0.0.1 and takes its address from its own GUI setting, not from the
  environment: `launchctl setenv OLLAMA_HOST 0.0.0.0:11434` was measured on 2026-09-09 to
  leave the relaunched app still on `TCP 127.0.0.1:11434 (LISTEN)`. A loopback listener is
  unreachable from the tailnet, so home 3 did not exist. Asking the founder to tick a box in
  a GUI is a hand on his machine every reinstall (LAW 31, R52), so this job owns the server
  instead: the same `ollama serve`, bound where the tunnel can reach it, restarted by launchd
  if it dies and started again at login.

  It is NOT a recurring job, so it is not a second scheduler and bin/idp-one-scheduler has
  nothing to fold in (THE HEADLINE): KeepAlive means "this daemon stays up", not "run this on
  a timer". Dagster remains the estate's one scheduler.

  Reach is fenced by the tailnet, not by the bind: platform/tailscale/policy.hujson is
  deny-by-default and admits only tag:k8s to tag:founder-mac:11434. 0.0.0.0 also exposes the
  port to whatever local network the laptop is on, which is the honest cost of Ollama.app
  having no per-interface bind; the macOS application firewall is the control for that and is
  the founder's to keep on.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>ai.estate.otto-home3</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/local/bin/ollama</string>
    <string>serve</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>OLLAMA_HOST</key>
    <string>0.0.0.0:11434</string>
    <!-- The lifeboat answers the founder, so a model stays resident rather than paying a
         cold load on the one turn that matters. Measured 2026-09-10: warm 12.7s, cold over
         120s. -1 is "never unload": the founder's laptop pays that load once after a reboot,
         and never on the message he sends while the cluster is down. -->
    <key>OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE</key>
    <string>-1</string>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>${PATH}</string>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>${HOME}/Library/Logs/ai.estate.otto-home3.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>${HOME}/Library/Logs/ai.estate.otto-home3.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
